WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.020
James Cameron has been promising a series
of Avatar sequels for roughly a decade, and

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.560
audiences are still waiting.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.820
“And so now you're worried about the sequels
that are coming out?"

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.490
We've already heard quite a few tidbits about
what the upcoming films will entail — and

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.980
we've rounded up all the rumors and spoilers
right here.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.650
James Cameron clearly wasn't interested in
churning out another Avatar sequel just for

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.320
the sake of it.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.600
Since 2010, he's been dropping hints about
what the future of the franchise involves

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.460
— and it's an increasingly ungainly vision
that includes several movie sequels, novels,

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.280
and much more.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.840
Details are often frustratingly vague — heck,
even the release dates keep changing.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.920
In fact, trying to pin down exactly when we'll
get to see Avatar 2 and its many sequels is

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.040
something of a fool's errand.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:51.460
Back in 2010, Cameron said the next two films
would be coming out in December 2014 and December

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.900
2015, respectively.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.680
But when January 2015 rolled around with no
sign of Avatar 2, he said the sequels had

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.660
been delayed… but they'd be coming out in
2017 — probably.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.820
Later in 2015, Cameron also hinted that there'd
be an Avatar 5.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.860
In April 2016, James Cameron told folks at
Comic Con:

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.220
"The next time I see you will be on Pandora."

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.010
He also claimed that Christmastime would officially
be Avatar-time… because Avatar 2 would be

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.140
coming out on Christmas 2018.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.020
Of course, that didn't happen.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.100
Then, in April 2017, the timeline shifted
again — and Cameron announced we could expect

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.920
Avatar 2 on December 18th, 2020.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.260
Is your head spinning yet?

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.020
"If you feel light-headed or dizzy -- "

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:34.520
"Ooohhh"

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.520
"You're wiggling your toes!"

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.300
"That's good."

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.980
December 18th, 2020 was the official word
for another two years — but that all changed

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.780
on May 2019.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.800
After Disney acquired Fox — the studio that
had previously owned Avatar — it was announced

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.300
that,

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.820
"Four forthcoming Avatar films, expanding
the vibrant world of Pandora, will release

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.900
on the pre-Christmas weekend every other year
beginning in 2021."

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.160
That's the story for now, anyway.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.620
"Avatar 2, 3, 4, 5…"

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.080
'Are you really?"

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.920
"Seriously, they're all written.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.360
And we've done the capture."

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.260
We still don't know for sure what the official
title of Avatar 2 will be.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.210
At one point, James Cameron reportedly didn't
even want the word 'avatar' in future installments

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:18.760
of the series.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:24.180
In 2012, he pointed out that Jake left his
avatar to become a real Na'Vi at the end of

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:24.680
Avatar.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:32.680
"Whatever happens tonight, either way, I'm
never coming back to this place."

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.420
Because of this major plot development, Cameron
claimed the term "avatar" no longer applies

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.220
to the series.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.700
But perhaps he's had a change of heart.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.280
Or perhaps he was strongarmed by studio brass
into keeping the word "avatar" in the film

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:45.780
titles.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:52.280
In 2018, the BBC claimed they'd seen documents
that referred to four upcoming Avatar projects

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:53.000
that were called:

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.520
Avatar: The Way of Water

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.260
Avatar: The Seed Bearer

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.060
Avatar: The Tulkun Rider

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.100
And, last but certainly not least,

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.040
Avatar: The Quest for Eywa

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.280
Of course, as with all things Avatar, all
these titles should be taken with an unusually

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.380
large grain of salt.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:13.880
James Cameron has said that most of what we'll
see onscreen in the four Avatar sequels is

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.960
motion-capture footage.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:21.040
His team reportedly started filming back in
September 2017, working on Avatar 2 and Avatar

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.990
3 back-to-back… as well as scenes for the
fourth installment.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:29.020
At an IMAX Q&amp;A in February 2019, producer
Jon Landau revealed:

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:32.880
“We’re going to do our live-action filming
in New Zealand in the spring of this year."

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.340
Then, in an interview with Empire that same
month, James Cameron revealed:

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.760
"That pesky little live-action component is
going to cost me five months of my life, across

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:42.640
the two movies."

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:48.000
We expected to see Sam Worthington and Zoe
Saldana return for the Avatar sequels… but

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.220
we were quite surprised to hear that Sigourney
Weaver and Stephen Lang are reportedly returning

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.720
for all four films, too.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.910
After all, both characters were supposedly
killed off in the first film: Dr. Grace Augustine

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:04.120
was struck by a fatal bullet, and Colonel
Quaritch was hit by two arrows fired by Saldana's

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.020
character, Neytiri.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.120
Weaver claims she'll be playing a different
character in the upcoming movies, but James

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.460
Cameron confirmed that Lang will somehow be
returning as the ill-willed colonel.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:18.300
In fact, he'll supposedly be the primary villain
in future films — which isn't to say he

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.220
was a sweetheart in the original Avatar.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.900
"You crossed a line."

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.720
In October 2017, it was revealed that Oscar-winning
actress Kate Winslet had been cast as a character

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:30.460
named Ronal.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.120
Talking to Vanity Fair in 2017, Cameron said:

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.500
"She’s very excited.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.840
She plays a character who’s part of the
Sea People, the reef people.

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.720
The one thing she did do is demand that she
do all her own water work."

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:47.180
The fact that Cameron and Winslet are working
together again may raise a few eyebrows.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.889
After all, their experience filming Titanic
didn't exactly sound like smooth sailing — no

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:52.380
pun intended.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.680
Reportedly, Winslet was often afraid that
she'd drown while filming Titanic, and she

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.100
once said of Cameron:

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.900
"There were times when I was genuinely frightened
of him.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.100
Jim has a temper like you wouldn’t believe."

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.159
But producer Jon Landau claims Winslet took
to her watery scenes in the Avatar sequels

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.220
like… well, like a duck takes to water.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.600
He told Collider:

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.479
"Kate Winslet had to train in this and she
got up to a static breath hold of just about

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:18.479
seven minutes.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.460
It’s amazing, it’s mind over matter.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.780
You see Kate going underwater and she just
felt so comfortable."

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:25.940
That's no small feat.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:32.460
In 2017, it was announced that Game of Thrones
actress Oona Chaplin would be playing a character

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.420
named Varang.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.770
Deadline reported that:

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:39.420
"[Varang is] a strong and vibrant central
character who spans the entire saga of the

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:39.920
sequels."

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:44.920
In March 2019, the official Avatar Twitter
account posted that Chaplin would be joined

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.240
by a fellow former Game of Thrones cast member.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.040
"Run away, little Theon.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.420
It's what you do best."

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.200
The tweet reads:

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:58.499
"Brendan Cowell has been cast in the Avatar
sequels as Mick Scoresby, captain of a large-scale

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.360
marine hunting vessel on Pandora."

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:06.439
And here's more great news for you: on February
6th, 2019, an announcement on the Avatar Twitter

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.439
account revealed,

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:12.120
"We are thrilled to share that Edie Falco
is joining the #AvatarFamily as General Ardmore,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.800
the Commander in charge of the RDA's interests
in the Avatar Sequels!

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.360
Are you as excited as we are?"

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:23.440
During an IMAX Q&amp;A in February 2019, producer
Jon Landau praised that particular casting

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:23.940
choice:

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:28.240
"In typical Jim [Cameron] fashion, he finds
this powerful woman to play what could be

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.780
very easily [be] a male role if people were
just to read the script."

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:36.879
Two months later, it was announced that Michelle
Yeoh of Crazy Rich Asians would play a scientist

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.160
named Dr. Karina Mogue.

00:06:38.749 --> 00:06:39.880
James Cameron tweeted,

00:06:39.889 --> 00:06:43.139
"Michelle has always created unique and memorable
characters.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:47.040
I look forward to working with her to do the
same thing on the Avatar sequels."

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.240
Avatar's official Twitter feed isn't the only
social media account buzzing with exciting

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.020
casting news.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:59.440
On April 3rd, 2019, Fast &amp; Furious star Vin
Diesel posted a video to his Instagram account:

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:04.779
“[There is one person in Hollywood that
I've always wanted to work with and learn

00:07:04.779 --> 00:07:06.250
from, and… where is he?"

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.160
"Yeah, where is that guy?"

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:12.280
Of course, that strongly implied Diesel would
be appearing in at least one of the Avatar

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:12.780
sequels.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.180
The actor later confirmed his involvement
while speaking to Entertainment Tonight at

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.260
the Avengers: Endgame premiere in April 2019.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.050
By the sound of it, he's super-excited to
be reunited with a certain co-star.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:30.660
"My favorite in the whole cast, or the closest
to my family, is Zoe Saldana… hence Avatar,

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.280
hence why I'm doing Avatar."

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:37.720
At the moment, Diesel's IMDb page only lists
his upcoming role in Avatar 2 as "rumored."

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:43.080
If he is in the film, you might have to be
especially eagle-eyed to spot him.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.660
Motion capture is tricky like that.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:49.899
Speaking to Empire, James Cameron revealed
that a large chunk of Avatar 2 will focus

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.060
on Jake and Neytiri's eight-year-old daughter.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:56.719
He also revealed that Jake and Neytiri are
still a couple, and a crucial plot point involves

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.120
a huge disagreement between the two lovebirds.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.060
"And you may choose a woman.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.560
We have many fine women."

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.860
In fact, the audience is apparently going
to watch this fight play out through the eyes

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:13.380
of their daughter.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:17.260
It sounds like there will be lots of child
actors in the Avatar sequels.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:22.080
In 2017, we were introduced to seven kids
who will be playing various Na'vi — either

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:27.960
from Neytiri's Omaticaya clan, or the Metkayina,
a community of ocean dwellers who evidently

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:28.740
live on reefs.

00:08:29.389 --> 00:08:33.880
As Cameron explained, he now sees the Avatar
films as a family saga — one that's akin

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:34.960
to the Godfather movies.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:40.060
He says that introducing kids into the action
signifies a major shift in perspective for

00:08:40.069 --> 00:08:44.000
the adult characters… because now they have
to consider how their actions will affect

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:44.500
their families.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:45.800
As he tells it:

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:50.640
"[Avatar 2 is] a continuation of the same
characters… but what happens when warriors

00:08:50.649 --> 00:08:55.160
who are willing to go on suicide charges and
leap off cliffs, what happens when they grow

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.420
up and have their own kids?

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:58.300
It becomes a very different story."

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:02.680
At least two stars will be on their home turf
while shooting the live-action scenes for

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.920
the new Avatar films.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.580
We're talking about New Zealand here, not
Pandora.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:11.560
Outside of his home country, Cliff Curtis
is best known for playing Travis in the AMC

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.180
spinoff series Fear the Walking Dead.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.000
He'll be playing the character of Tonowari,
the leader of the Metkayina.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.180
Curtis told Newstalk ZB that he didn't even
have to audition:

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.700
"[I got] a phone call from James Cameron.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:25.180
That turned into a Skype call and he offered
me four movies.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:26.500
It was that simple.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.900
It was a straight invitation."

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:32.860
There's one more New Zealander heading off
to Pandora: actor, writer, and director Jemaine

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:33.360
Clement.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:38.400
You may recognize him as one half of the comedy
duo Flight of the Conchords, or perhaps you've

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:42.120
seen his work on the 2014 vampire comedy What
We Do in the Shadows.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:47.380
Clement is also an executive producer on the
FX series of the same name, which is loosely

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.740
based on the film, of course.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:54.680
“The hardest thing about making a show like
this is not being bitten by vampires."

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:58.060
On May 15th, the official Avatar Twitter account
announced:

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.880
"Jemaine Clement has been cast in the Avatar
sequels as Dr. Garvin, a marine biologist

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:03.620
on Pandora.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:04.840
Glad to have you aboard"

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:10.660
In 2010, Jon Landau told MTV that James Cameron
was planning to write a novel that offers

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:13.320
more insight into the various characters'
backgrounds.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:17.760
Specifically, he said that we'd be hearing
a lot about Dr. Augustine's time teaching

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.640
in the schoolhouse.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.300
"This was our school…

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:23.140
Now it's just storage."

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:27.580
We'd also learn more details about Jake's
identical twin brother Tommy.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.000
"Jesus, Tommy."

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.519
"The strong prey on the weak.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.380
A guy with a knife took all Tommy would ever
be."

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:40.000
Landau noted that it wouldn't be a novelization
of the first movie, but a separate story that

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.280
goes into far more detail than the first film.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:46.820
Cameron confirmed this, saying that he'd always
intended to write a novel if Avatar ever made

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:47.400
any money.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.100
Which it most certainly did.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.280
But as plans for the follow-up films stalled,
plans for the book evidently stalled, too.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:59.520
Then, in 2017, The Los Angeles Times reported
that Penguin Random House was teaming up with

00:10:59.529 --> 00:11:03.639
Cameron to release a whole slew of books based
on Avatar… stories that would be geared

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.540
towards children and adults alike.

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:10.260
The first books are expected to come out just
before the Avatar 2 premiere… which means

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.780
we still have to wait awhile before we can
read them.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.879
If you enjoyed the colorful visuals of Pandora,
you'll be pleased to know that the next four

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.740
films are all going to be set there, too.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.480
In an IMAX Q&amp;A, producer Jon Landau said,

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:27.100
"We realized that if we looked at Earth, we
could spend our whole life traveling the globe

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:28.420
[...]. Let’s do that on Pandora.

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:33.660
Let Pandora really truly be that metaphor
where we get to go see all these incredible

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:34.540
different environments."

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:39.480
Meanwhile, a lot of the action in Avatar 2
takes place underwater — which reportedly

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:41.580
led to a number of production hitches.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.840
In November 2017, Cameron noted that,

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:49.180
"Basically, whenever you add water to any
problem, it just gets ten times harder."

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:54.200
With any luck, we'll be able to enjoy these
Avatar sequels before our entire planet is

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:54.700
underwater.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:57.660
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.920
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

